  "description": "An expectation requires A-602 to show Door 102's fire rating as \"90 min\", and A-602's Monday issue shows \"1.5 h\". A Wednesday normalization of the project names the fixture fire-rating interpretation. The property is fulfilled on Wednesday, not on Monday: the normalization's write records its end act at Wednesday, citing the Monday evidence, with the interpretation and matched_by the normalization. A Tuesday read shows it outstanding. A second expectation, whose context names the fixture accept-empty interpretation, is untouched by the normalization: read under its own interpretation it stays outstanding, and the normalization's write records nothing for it.",
  "note": "6.5.1: the qualifying moment is the latest of the evidence's occurrence time, the establishment time \"and, for evidence that meets the value requirement only under an interpretation that a normalization put in force (7.3.8), the instant from which that interpretation is in force for the subject ... fulfillment never reaches back before the normalization ... Where the evidence meets the requirement only under an interpretation that a normalization put in force, the result also references that normalization, beside the evidence (5.5.4).\" 7.6.13: \"An expectation's interpretation is the one its context names, at every instant.\" 7.3.8: \"An expectation property whose period is open at T, whose interpretation is the one in force (7.6.13), and whose evidence meets its requirement only under the interpretation in force from T, is fulfilled no earlier than T, citing the normalization beside the evidence (6.5.1).\"",
